# Belated April and May Update!

Okay, so I kind of forgot to post an update last month! Oops, I knew I
was forgetting something!

In May there was a kindly contributed MA-3 music emulator donated to
SquirrelJME by the alias of _Guy Perfect_, which means that SquirrelJME will
soon get sound support for both MIDP and DoJa! I am currently working on
integrating this taking a break from NanoCoat's execution work to get this
into the standalone! Will definitely have an update once that is in!

There were some important compatibility improvements in April, which will
definitely improve things! SquirrelJME now changes the functionality of
certain API functions depending on the platform version requested by the
software. There have been changes over the course of both Java ME and DoJa
where the behavior of methods just changed! Now this is correctly handled
and as such, graphically everything looks far better and less glitchy!

The other major compatibility improvement is that the Record Management
System, or RMS, now is implemented in a proper way and is stored to disk. So
any data or progress that an application/game saves will be stored and
resumes. This also applies to DoJa as well!

There were additional minor compatibility fixes with DoJa due to some
software requiring very lenient scratchpad behavior, as such this has been
additionally applied to SquirrelJME. This mostly fixes the Legacy of Network
and Phantom of Network games.

The number pad now properly works and inverts accordingly so that it matches
the layout of the dial-pad, since keyboard number pads have the calculator
layout.

Work on NanoCoat code execution continues, not much to say there!
